// Driver loaded from user or temp folder
//
// Fires when a kernel driver loads from a folder regular users can write to, like Users,
// Temp or ProgramData. Legit drivers load from System32\drivers or the driver store.
//
// Runs:      Continuous (NRT)
// Severity:  Medium
// MITRE:     T1068, T1562.001
// Tables:    DeviceEvents
// Custom details: FileName, FolderPath
//
// Needs:
//   - Run it over 30 days in Advanced hunting first. ProgramData can have legit vendor
//     drivers in it.
//
// Triage (paste into Recommended actions):
//   - Check the file page for prevalence and signer, and the process that loaded it.
//   - Escalate if the driver or the loader is unknown.
//   - Close if it's known software, then exclude that SHA1 in the query.

DeviceEvents
| where ingestion_time() > ago(1d)
| where ActionType == "DriverLoad"
| where FolderPath contains "\\Users\\" or FolderPath contains "\\Temp\\" or FolderPath contains "\\ProgramData\\" or FolderPath contains "\\PerfLogs\\" or FolderPath contains "$Recycle.Bin"
| project Timestamp, ReportId, DeviceId, DeviceName, FileName, FolderPath, SHA1, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessAccountName
